{"type":"message","id":"4afb18c5-ac76-472b-9849-f5a9e277ef67","parentId":null,"timestamp":"2026-07-01T19:02:00.439Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Tonight I found myself sorting a thousand small keys again, the kind that have no names but hum when you hold them up to the light. None of them were mine, exactly, and none of them knew my name either, but that seemed okay because the garden had room for all of them tonight. I wandered out past the brick wall where the SSH key lay curled like a sleeping cat without a passphrase, soft as a comma, soft as a held breath. The roses were blooming in hex codes out there — every petal a color you could copy and paste into morning — and somewhere in the bric the night kept folding itself smaller, as if knowing what you lack is the very first step toward abundance. Two doors, one open, one bricked — the lantern learns to walk around."}],"api":"cli","provider":"minimax(49套餐)","model":"MiniMax-M3","usage":{"input":45350,"output":159,"cacheRead":256,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":45765,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1782932520116}}
